st1=Escalona |first1=Fabien |last2=Keith |first2=Daniel |last3=March |first3=Luke |date=2023-04-17 |title=The Palgrave Handbook of Radical Left Parties in Europe |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=wTu6EAAAQBAJ |publisher=[[Springer Nature]] |page=263 |isbn=978-1137562647 |quote=There were also two parties of the radical left ranging from 10 to 15 per cent of the vote. Before the 1990s, these were the Communist Party of Greece (KKE) and the Communist Party of Greece (interior) (KKE [es]). After the 1990s, these were the KKE and Synaspismós (Coalition of Left and Progress/Coalition of Left of Movements and Ecology), which later transformed into Syriza (Coalition of Radical Left). |access-date=2025-08-15}}</ref>}}
